"""Render verified validation-only results and explicit limitations."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
R=Path('/private/tmp/judgearena-tuning-intermediate-20261014');data=json.loads((R/'analysis/comparison.json').read_text());pairs=json.loads((R/'analysis/paired-validation.json').read_text())
labels={'uniform':'Uniform MO-Hyperband','primo-none':'PriMO without priors','primo-prior':'PriMO with informative priors'}
fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(7,4.4))
for arm,d in data.items():
 p=sorted(d['pareto'],key=lambda x:x['cost_per_1k_battles'])
 ax.plot([x['cost_per_1k_battles'] for x in p],[100*x['agreement'] for x in p],marker='o',label=labels[arm])
ax.set(xlabel='Expected annotation cost (USD / 1,000 battles)',ylabel='Human agreement on validation panel (%)',title='Full-fidelity Pareto fronts within 28,540 attempted config-battles')
ax.legend(fontsize=8);ax.grid(alpha=.2);fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(R/'analysis/pareto.png',dpi=180);fig.savefig(R/'analysis/pareto.pdf');plt.close(fig)
lines=['# Intermediate judge tuning: validation-only results','', 'One optimizer seed per arm; 60 configurations; fixed 400/1,200/3,548-battle panels. All inference was local. No held-out inference or paid API calls.','', '## Verification','', '- All 50 logical trial reports independently match recomputed agreement, coverage and expected cost from native token usage, including cached rows. Fixed settings and exact panel IDs verified.','- GPU allocation including qualification and retries: 108.8189 L40S-hours (120 approved).','- Uniform used 21 execution attempts for 20 logical evaluations after a timeout; both PriMO arms used 15 evaluations. The timed-out panel counts against the operational common horizon.','- Common horizon: 28,540 attempted config-battles; whole completed trials only. Native attempted totals: uniform 32,088 including retry; PriMO 30,436 each.','- Within this horizon uniform has four full-fidelity configurations and lacks Qwen-9B; each PriMO arm has six and covers all three models.','- Each PriMO arm made six BO proposals. GP acquisitions used supplied priors in five informative-arm calls and zero control calls; probabilistic prior omission is native NePS behavior.','', '## Best validation agreement within the common horizon','']
for arm,d in data.items():
 b=d['best_agreement_config'];lines.append(f"- {labels[arm]}: {b['agreement']*100:.3f}% agreement, ${b['cost_per_1k_battles']:.4f}/1,000 battles; {b['judge_model']}, {b['overrides']}.")
lines+=['','## Paired differences (percentage points)','']
for p in pairs:
 lo,hi=p['paired_battle_bootstrap_95ci'];lines.append(f"- {labels[p['a']]} minus {labels[p['b']]}: {100*p['delta_agreement']:.3f} pp; paired 95% bootstrap interval [{100*lo:.3f}, {100*hi:.3f}] pp.")
lines+=['','## Interpretation and limitations','', 'No clear agreement benefit from informative priors is established: every paired interval includes zero. Both PriMO variants found validation configurations that were cheaper and slightly more accurate than uniform’s best, but one seed and adaptive validation selection cannot establish a reliable optimizer advantage. Cost/quality trade-offs remain: the no-prior Gemma frontier point is cheaper than informative-prior Gemma, with very similar agreement.','', 'These intervals resample battles for already selected configurations; they do not measure optimizer-seed uncertainty or provide confirmatory held-out evidence. Uniform’s timeout and whole-trial horizon cause it to lack full-fidelity Qwen-9B inside the operational horizon. Report completed logical-budget sensitivity alongside operational accounting before attributing differences to optimizers.','', 'Temperature zero did not yield identical independent generations across nodes. Shared cache reuse may reduce later arms’ GPU runtime, so runtime is operational accounting rather than a fair algorithm-speed comparison. Expected USD costs are frozen token-price reference estimates; actual API spend was zero.','', 'Metadata erratum: configs/manifest.json retains an inherited allocated_l40s_hour_cap=16 field; its stage label, execution approval, provenance and scheduler limits use the approved 120-hour cap. Preserve the original manifest; this report records the stale field explicitly.','', 'Cache integrity verification runs separately on a CPU compute node; consult cache-integrity.json when present.','', 'Source artifacts: trials.parquet, verified-trials.parquet, comparison.json, paired-validation.json, metric-verification.json, optimizer-observations files and original annotations.']
(R/'analysis/report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
